        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(dispatch-wrapper): fix flock separator and script command detection",
        "body": "Related: #98964\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\n1. **flock `--` separator**: `flock /tmp/lock -- echo hello` was not unwrapped because `--` was treated as an option-like token. Now skipped as POSIX separator between lock target and command.\n\n2. **script command misdetection**: `script -- echo hello` mislabeled `echo` as a transcript file. Now detects `--` separator form (all tokens are command) vs transcript-file form (first token is transcript, rest is command). Transcript-only invocations like `script -q /dev/null` stay blocked.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n- flock: detect `--` after lock target and skip past it\n- script: check if `--` was consumed by the scanner to distinguish command-only from transcript-file forms\n\n## User Impact\n\nFixes command execution analysis for `flock` and `script` invocations with `--` separator.\n\n## Evidence\n\n![proof](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/zhangLei99586/openclaw/proof-screenshots/pr-98657-proof.png)\n\n- `exec-wrapper-resolution.test.ts`: 132/132 passed ✅\n- `exec-approvals-allow-always.test.ts`: 48/48 passed ✅",
        "branch": "fix/flock-dashdash-separator",
        "head_sha": "fe5e06d5556885a33e96dc3856179549bbb57e7d",
